WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.335
This is Jason.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:05.505
He has more than
2,500 band shirts,

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.258
enjoys 80s thrash metal albums,

00:00:09.884 --> 00:00:12.220
has a dog named Bela Lugosi,

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.431
drinks black coffee
in the morning.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.934
And I sue government
agencies for information.

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:27.736
I'm Jason Leopold

00:00:27.736 --> 00:00:29.529
and I'm an
investigative journalist.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:33.074
Money laundering, corruption,

00:00:33.074 --> 00:00:34.909
covert programs.

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:37.412
Secret Service
visiting celebrities.

00:00:37.412 --> 00:00:39.622
I have the luxury of

00:00:39.622 --> 00:00:44.294
dipping my toe into any subject.

00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:48.298
I've been described as a
FOIA terrorist by the FBI.

00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:51.509
I've also been referred to as
a member of a FOIA posse

00:00:51.509 --> 00:00:53.595
by the Department of Justice.

00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:55.847
And the NSA has actually said
I've weaponized the FOIA.

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:05.023
The Freedom of Information Act,
which is commonly known as

00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:07.650
the FOIA, is a law
that gives you the right

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:10.320
to access information
from the federal government.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.781
It's a half-century-old law.

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:15.533
Often described as a law
that keeps citizens in the know

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:17.410
about what their
government is doing.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:21.289
It's an incredibly powerful tool.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:25.085
So I first got involved with the
Freedom of Information Act,

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.420
probably about 15 years ago.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.674
And really where
it started to pick up

00:01:31.674 --> 00:01:34.135
was during Occupy Wall Street.

00:01:34.135 --> 00:01:38.932
I started to file requests with
the FBI related to their role

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:42.644
in allegedly dismantling
the encampments

00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:45.188
that were set up
around the country.

00:01:45.188 --> 00:01:48.316
Remarkably, the FBI responds
to my FOIA request

00:01:48.316 --> 00:01:50.360
by stating they had no records

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:52.946
and they could not
locate any records.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:56.825
So, I had hooked up
with an attorney.

00:01:56.825 --> 00:02:00.370
And he told me, well,
we can sue the agency.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.496
We can sue the FBI.

00:02:01.496 --> 00:02:02.914
And I was like, wait what?

00:02:02.914 --> 00:02:04.958
I can sue the government?

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.919
Uh, where do I sign up?

00:02:07.919 --> 00:02:09.796
And wouldn't you
know, once I sued them,

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.214
they found those records

00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:13.675
that they said they could not find.

00:02:13.675 --> 00:02:15.093
And from that moment on,

00:02:15.093 --> 00:02:17.720
I just kind of kept filing requests

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:19.305
and suing the government.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.683
I'm constantly
filing FOIA requests.

00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:24.561
I've easily filed more than 5,000.

00:02:24.561 --> 00:02:26.771
There are instances
where I'll be driving

00:02:26.771 --> 00:02:29.482
and I'll hear something
on the radio and I need to

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:32.443
pull over because I have
to get the request filed.

00:02:32.443 --> 00:02:33.695
Really, what I'm trying to do

00:02:33.695 --> 00:02:37.115
is to pry loose records so
I can build out investigations,

00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:42.120
but also trying to get records
that would enlighten the public

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.081
and shed light on
hot-button issues.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:50.503
I think the FOIA is underutilized

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:52.255
by the general public.

00:02:52.255 --> 00:02:57.177
Journalists only make up
a sliver of requests that are filed

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.636
on the federal level.

00:02:58.636 --> 00:03:02.557
There's certainly been an
uptick in the use of FOIA

00:03:02.557 --> 00:03:04.726
over the past
decade or so.

00:03:04.726 --> 00:03:06.477
But the majority

00:03:06.477 --> 00:03:09.647
of the FOIA requests that
federal government agencies

00:03:09.647 --> 00:03:11.608
receive are from

00:03:11.608 --> 00:03:13.026
commercial requesters,

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:14.819
people who are taking that

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:16.738
information and selling it.

00:03:16.738 --> 00:03:18.990
They're not requesting records

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:20.909
that are in the public interest.

00:03:20.909 --> 00:03:23.328
They're not sharing those
records with the public.

00:03:23.328 --> 00:03:28.208
The FOIA request is what
I refer to as a template.

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:30.877
My template says,
this is a request

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:33.129
under the Freedom
of Information Act.

00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:36.674
And I cite the law and
I'm telling the agency

00:03:36.674 --> 00:03:38.885
exactly what I'm looking for.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:44.307
So it's a very simple process,
but it can also be painstaking.

00:03:44.307 --> 00:03:45.141
And here's why.

00:03:45.141 --> 00:03:49.187
Agencies are not so eager
to turn over records.

00:03:49.187 --> 00:03:51.397
And I just sit back and wait.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:54.275
But sometimes waiting
can take years.

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:58.279
It's like Christmas
when I get these.

00:03:58.279 --> 00:04:01.407
Whoa, whoa.

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:05.078
US Treasury, Financial Crimes
Enforcement Network.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:08.706
And this is a request

00:04:08.706 --> 00:04:12.543
that I actually filed back in 2017.

00:04:12.543 --> 00:04:17.131
So, it's taken the
agency about six years.

00:04:17.131 --> 00:04:18.883
There really is no
general wait time.

00:04:18.883 --> 00:04:23.096
There's more than 400
federal government agencies.

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:27.517
So depending on the agency,
the requests can take anywhere

00:04:27.517 --> 00:04:30.478
from three months to ten years.

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:31.896
The least amount of time

00:04:31.896 --> 00:04:35.483
that I've waited for documents
was about two days.

00:04:35.483 --> 00:04:39.237
I would say that the record
of documents that arrived

00:04:39.237 --> 00:04:40.905
on my doorstep

00:04:40.905 --> 00:04:44.075
in one day was probably
about 7,000 pages

00:04:44.075 --> 00:04:45.952
from the State Department.

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:49.205
And I think that they did
that as a **** you to me,

00:04:49.205 --> 00:04:52.959
knowing that I'd have to thumb
through each and every page.

00:04:53.584 --> 00:04:57.005
The request that had
the most impact

00:04:57.005 --> 00:05:00.591
and I mean the most impact

00:05:00.591 --> 00:05:03.511
was for Hillary Clinton's emails.

00:05:03.511 --> 00:05:06.431
We are all accountable to
the American people to get

00:05:06.431 --> 00:05:08.558
the facts right.

00:05:08.558 --> 00:05:10.560
And it was my request

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:14.230
and my lawsuit that became
the vehicle by which

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.524
all of Hillary Clinton's
emails were released.

00:05:16.774 --> 00:05:17.817
And by the way like,

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.861
I had no idea she
had a private server.

00:05:19.861 --> 00:05:21.863
I was just trying to get
the public to be like,

00:05:21.863 --> 00:05:24.157
Hey! Look, it’s her emails.

00:05:24.157 --> 00:05:24.991
Anyway.

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:28.578
The FBI has uncovered new
evidence in its investigation

00:05:28.578 --> 00:05:30.747
of Democratic presidential
nominee Hillary Clinton's

00:05:30.747 --> 00:05:32.790
use of a private email server.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:35.501
Donald Trump is praising
the FBI's decision

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:37.211
to review new emails.

00:05:37.211 --> 00:05:41.174
Another FOIA request that I
filed and ultimately a lawsuit

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:44.344
that resulted in
thousands of records

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:46.304
that were released
that had enormous

00:05:46.304 --> 00:05:51.017
impact were records around
Robert Mueller's report into

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:53.811
whether or not Trump
had colluded with Russia

00:05:53.811 --> 00:05:57.190
during the campaign of 2016.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:00.693
I was able to get
Donald Trump Jr's name

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:03.529
unredacted from
the Mueller Report.

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:07.325
I've gotten records
from the government

00:06:07.325 --> 00:06:11.245
where they talked ****
about me in emails.

00:06:11.245 --> 00:06:13.873
And one time,

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:17.418
the FBI sent an agent out

00:06:17.418 --> 00:06:20.630
to investigate one
of my FOIA requests

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:22.590
and I only found out about that

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.801
because I filed a FOIA
request with the FBI.

00:06:26.177 --> 00:06:29.972
The most rewarding part of this
job has always been holding

00:06:29.972 --> 00:06:33.935
power to account and
speaking truth to power.

00:06:33.935 --> 00:06:37.438
That is really what
keeps me going.

00:06:37.438 --> 00:06:42.110
And being able to shine
a light into dark places.

